# `burxt fetch` writes these; the LOCKFILE is what gets committed, not the checkout.
.burxt/

# The tools, built from their sources in examples/.
star-generate
star-check
star-build
star-liquid
star-limits
star-surface
star-content
star-collection
star-reachable

# **Generated beside their source, and the NEGATIONS are the load-bearing part.** `examples/*.bx`
# alone also swallows the three tools' own sources, which live here too — and a new source file that
# is silently untracked is the worst shape this can take: it builds locally forever and CI has never
# seen it. So the generated shapes are ignored and the sources are named back in.
examples/*.bx
!examples/generate.bx
!examples/check.bx
!examples/build.bx
# **Added after this rule's own warning came true.** `prove-partition.bx` was written, built, verified
# against the JavaScript it replaced on both success and failure, committed with `git add -A` — and
# silently not added, because `examples/*.bx` swallowed it and nothing names it back in. `main` went red
# on `cannot read examples/prove-partition.bx`, and the comment four lines above had described exactly
# that outcome: *"a new source file that is silently untracked is the worst shape this can take: it
# builds locally forever and CI has never seen it."*
!examples/prove-partition.bx
examples/*.check.bx
# **And the same thing one line down, found the same way.** `examples/theme.css` is hand-written — the
# page-level half of star's design system, documented on `docs/how-do-i.md`, read by the gallery and by
# `star-reachable` — and it has never been committed. A fresh clone of this repository fails with
# `ENOENT: examples/theme.css`. Nothing could see it: CI has no gallery step, and every developer machine
# has the file. It took cloning the repository and following CLAUDE.md's own build block.
#
# `star-languages` now holds this rule by provenance rather than by list: everything star generates under
# `examples/` is generated from a document, so an ignored `examples/X.ext` is an artefact exactly when
# `examples/X.sbmx` exists. Sixteen ignored files here, fifteen with a document, and this was the one
# without.
examples/*.css
!examples/theme.css
examples/*.o
examples/*.wasm
star-languages
star-refs
star-showcase
star-guarantees
star-consuming
star-pack

# Python leaves these behind; nothing here should be tracking them.
__pycache__/
star-docs
star-partition
star-lsp
star-drive-lsp

# **Andre's golden rules, and how this work is run.** Local on purpose: it is how the work is done
# rather than part of the product, and it is the same file in every repository in the family.
.claude/
star-versions
star-workflows
star-controls
star-flags
